Known limits
shortcut: transfers move stock in one step. Add an in-transit state if transfers take days.
shortcut: reconciliation dates use UTC. Add a business-date column if stores close at local midnight.
shortcut: promotions are automatic. There are no coupon codes or per-customer limits.
shortcut: one currency per order. There is no conversion.
SQLite allows one writer at a time. BEGIN IMMEDIATE makes this safe. For high write volume, port db.py to Postgres: change the placeholders to %s or $n, use SELECT ... FOR UPDATE where a row is read before a guarded update, and keep the guarded UPDATE statements as they are.
